[h1]Dynamic Trade Blackhole — Break the 1444 Trade Rails[/h1]

[quote]
[b]"Tired of the English Channel, Genoa, and Venice always sucking the entire world's wealth dry no matter how powerful Ming, Hindustan, or the New World becomes?"[/b]
[/quote]

For over a decade in [i]Europa Universalis IV[/i], global commerce has been bolted onto 1444 railroad tracks. Even if you forge a 3,000-development superpower in East Asia, India, Persia, Africa, or the Americas, the arrows painted on the map still force your hard-earned trade value downstream toward Western Europe.

[b]Dynamic Trade Blackhole[/b] shatters the fixed 1444 trade map. Powered by the [b]Foch[/b] runtime host, this mod makes EU4's trade network [b]alive, responsive, and reversible[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]Wealth Follows Economic Gravity:[/b] Outgoing trade routes dynamically close when a node's domestic purchasing power outgrows its downstream neighbor—preventing richer regions from draining into poorer ones.
[*][b]Emergent End-Nodes ("Trade Black Holes"):[/b] When all outgoing routes from a trade hub close, it becomes an [b]emergent end-node[/b] that retains 100% of its trade value. Even from a 1444 start, powerhouses like [b]Malacca, Coromandel, and Gujarat[/b] can naturally earn black-hole status—or you can develop [b]Nippon[/b] to seal off its leak to Hangzhou!
[*][b]Reversible Trade Corridors:[/b] No closure is permanent. Push massive trade power and steering back across a dormant corridor, and the route [b]dynamically reopens[/b].
[*][b]Collectors, Middlemen & Producers All Get Paid:[/b] Vanilla EU4 only rewards the final collector. Here, transit hubs earn monthly [b]Transit Fees[/b] and manufacturing heartlands earn [b]Source Bounties[/b] straight into their national treasuries.
[/list]

