[h2]Core Gameplay Features[/h2]

[h3]1. Every Development Click Shapes Global Trade Routes[/h3]
Instead of forcing you to conquer half a continent downstream just to stop your ducats from leaking away, [b]Dynamic Trade Blackhole[/b] turns province development and trade fleets into strategic geo-economic levers:
[list]
[*][b]Tax & Manpower Development (Build Domestic Purchasing Power):[/b] A node's internal absorption ("sink signal") grows with its provinces' [b]Tax[/b] and [b]Manpower[/b] (counted at half weight to represent population consumption). When your node's purchasing power equals or exceeds a downstream neighbor's and net outflow drops below the close threshold ([code]flow_epsilon_pct[/code], default [b]5%[/b]), that outgoing route closes!
[*][b]Production Development (Fuel Local Trade Value):[/b] Developing production injects fresh local goods value into the node's pool, shifting both local retention and export volume.
[*][b]Trade Power & Steering (Reopen Dormant Corridors):[/b] Closed routes are never deleted from the game. If downstream merchants and trade fleets drive net forward flow back above the reopen threshold ([code]reopen_pct[/code], default [b]15%[/b]) for consecutive months, the route [b]reopens[/b] automatically.
[/list]

[h3]2. Three Distinct Economic Roles — Stop Getting Robbed Upstream![/h3]
In vanilla EU4, if you don't own the end-node, your production and steering mostly enrich someone else. This mod splits each node's monthly outflow by origin into two non-overlapping fee pools distributed proportionally by trade power share directly to national treasuries:

[table]
[tr]
[th]Economic Role[/th]
[th]Primary Player Lever[/th]
[th]How You Profit[/th]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]1. The Sink (Collector)[/b][/td]
[td]Tax & Manpower Development[/td]
[td][b]Emergent End-Node Collection:[/b] Close outgoing routes so 100% of arriving and local trade value stays trapped inside your home node for collection.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]2. The Middleman (Transit Hub)[/b][/td]
[td]Trade Power & Steering[/td]
[td][b]Monthly Transit Fee (Default 20%):[/b] Earn a direct treasury cut of all trade volume your hub forwards on behalf of upstream nodes. Pure relay hubs finally get paid like real historical Silk Road and spice entrepôts![/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]3. The Producer (Source Heartland)[/b][/td]
[td]Production & Manufactories[/td]
[td][b]Monthly Source Bounty (Default 20%):[/b] Earn a direct treasury cut of your node's own local production when it is exported downstream—so manufacturing giants profit even when their goods travel abroad.[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]

[h3]3. Smooth 12-Month Moving Average "Trade Gazette" & Anti-Flicker Stability[/h3]
Worried about trade routes ping-ponging open and shut every single month? We engineered multi-layered stability controls so the global trade map evolves organically over years and eras:
[list]
[*][b]Hysteresis & Multi-Month Evidence Cooldowns:[/b] By default, a route only closes after net flow stays below [b]5%[/b] for [b]6 consecutive months[/b] ([code]evidence_months = 6[/code]), and only reopens after sustained flow climbs back above [b]15%[/b] for [b]6 consecutive months[/b]. Combined with a monthly global flip cap ([code]max_flips_total = 16[/code]), trade geography shifts deliberately and predictably.
[*][b]The World Trade Hub Gazette:[/b] Every month, all nodes are ranked by their true [b]Entrepôt Score[/b] (external trade value attracted × trade power, stripping out raw local production so pure resource regions don't masquerade as trade hubs). The Gazette tracks the [b]World Entrepôt[/b] (#1 global hub), [b]Great Entrepôts[/b] (Top 3), and [b]Regional Entrepôts[/b] (Top 8), logging historic announcements whenever a rising power dethrones the reigning World Entrepôt!
[*][b]12-Month Moving Average Benchmark:[/b] The Gazette tracks a rolling [b]12-month moving average[/b] of the world leader's entrepôt score alongside monthly corridor intelligence (including under-steered high-volume corridors and reopen progress diagnostics), smoothing out seasonal noise.
[/list]

[h3]4. Five Ready-to-Play Presets (Zero Manual Config Editing Required)[/h3]
Switch your campaign's economic feel anytime using the built-in preset tool ([code]tools/presets.py[/code]):

[table]
[tr]
[th]Preset Name[/th]
[th]Gameplay Feel[/th]
[th]Key Rules & Payouts[/th]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b][code]standard[/code][/b] [i](Recommended)[/i][/td]
[td][b]Balanced Default[/b] — Tuned across multi-year test campaigns for responsive yet grounded economic evolution.[/td]
[td]6 months evidence | Close < 5% / Reopen > 15% | Max 16 flips/mo | [b]20%[/b] Transit Fee & [b]20%[/b] Source Bounty[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b][code]gentle[/code][/b][/td]
[td][b]Grand Historical Pace[/b] — Trade routes only shift after sustained, generational economic transformations.[/td]
[td]12 months (1 full year) evidence | Close < 5% / Reopen > 20% | Max 8 flips/mo | [b]10%[/b] Transit Fee & [b]10%[/b] Source Bounty[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b][code]assertive[/code][/b][/td]
[td][b]Cutthroat Trade Warfare[/b] — Fast route flips and high rewards for aggressive development and fleet steering.[/td]
[td]4 months evidence | Close < 3% / Reopen > 12% | Max 24 flips/mo | [b]25%[/b] Transit Fee & [b]25%[/b] Source Bounty[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b][code]observer[/code][/b][/td]
[td][b]Pure Analytics Watch Mode[/b] — Keeps vanilla trade routes and treasuries 100% untouched while logging full monthly trade diagnostics.[/td]
[td][code]mode = "observe"[/code] | No route changes | No fee payouts | Full monthly observer logs enabled[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b][code]sandbox[/code][/b][/td]
[td][b]Safe First-Run Sanity Check[/b] — Master switch off so you can verify your Foch launch setup before enabling dynamic trade.[/td]
[td][code]enabled = false[/code] | Completely inert after startup verification[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]

Want fine-grained control? Advanced players can also customize individual parameters in [code]selections.toml[/code], including [code]sink_basis[/code] ([code]"mean"[/code] per-province wealth intensity so tall nations shine vs. [code]"sum"[/code] raw regional mass for sprawling empires), [code]relay_ref[/code], [code]flow_epsilon_pct[/code], [code]reopen_pct[/code], [code]evidence_months[/code], [code]max_flips_total[/code], [code]transit_fee_pct[/code], and [code]source_fee_pct[/code]. Any invalid manual edit safely auto-downgrades to observe-only mode instead of crashing!

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Built for Total Overhaul Mods (Anbennar, MEIOU & Taxes, Ante Bellum & More!)[/h2]

Most trade mods overwrite [code]common/tradenodes/00_tradenodes.txt[/code], instantly breaking every map overhaul on the Steam Workshop. [b]Dynamic Trade Blackhole never edits a single trade-node script file:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Zero Hardcoded Vanilla Nodes:[/b] Supports anywhere from [b]1 to 4,096 trade nodes[/b], up to [b]32,767 countries[/b], and up to [b]65,536 provinces per node[/b] out of the box.
[*][b]Plug-and-Play with Major Overhauls:[/b] Designed from day one to work naturally with [b]Anbennar[/b], [b]MEIOU & Taxes[/b], [b]Ante Bellum[/b], [b]Extended Timeline[/b], [b]Voltaire's Nightmare[/b], and any custom fantasy or alternate-history map.
[*][b]Dynamic Node Discovery + Playset [code]replace_path[/code] Support:[/b] The runtime automatically discovers trade nodes and province memberships dynamically, backed by an automatic fallback table ([code]node_members.txt[/code]). Using a heavy mod stack that reshapes trade regions? Run the included [code]tools/gen_members.py[/code] helper—it reads your exact EU4 launcher playset ([code]dlc_load.json[/code]), respects mod load order, reads [code].zip[/code] Workshop archives, and honors overhaul [code]replace_path[/code] directives automatically!
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Simple 3-Step Installation via Foch[/h2]

[h3]Why Does This Mod Use the Foch Runtime Loader?[/h3]
EU4's Clausewitz script engine has [b]no script command or trigger[/b] capable of adding, removing, or reversing trade-node arrows once a campaign starts. To make trade routes dynamically close and reopen during live gameplay without corrupting saves or conflicting with overhaul mods, this mod runs as a native plugin inside [b]Foch[/b] ([url=https://github.com/Acture/foch]GitHub: Acture/foch[/url]):
[list]
[*][b]100% Clean & Non-Invasive:[/b] Foch loads the plugin in an isolated runtime layer when launching the game. It [b]never patches, modifies, or overwrites your Steam [code]eu4.exe[/code] or any file in your EU4 installation folder[/b].
[*][b]One-Command Toggle:[/b] Disable or uninstall the plugin at any time with a single command and your base game remains completely untouched.
[*][b]Role of This Steam Workshop Item:[/b] Subscribe to this Workshop item to keep the companion mod in your playset and stay updated on release announcements, documentation, and presets, then activate the runtime plugin in 3 quick steps below.
[/list]

[h3]Step 1 — Install the Plugin (China Mirror Supported!)[/h3]
With [b]Foch CLI[/b] installed, download and install the plugin package (players in Mainland China can pass [code]--mirror cn[/code] or [code]--mirror auto[/code] for high-speed mirror acceleration):
[code]
# Automatic mirror selection:
foch plugin install Acture/eu4-dynamic-trade-blackhole --mirror auto

# Or force Mainland China mirror acceleration:
foch plugin install Acture/eu4-dynamic-trade-blackhole --mirror cn
[/code]
[i](Building from a local Foch workspace instead? Run [code]foch plugin import ./target/plugin-pkg[/code] after assembling the package.)[/i]

[h3]Step 2 — Enable the Plugin & Choose Your Preset[/h3]
Enable the plugin for your playset (e.g., [code]default[/code]) and optionally apply any of the 5 gameplay presets:
[code]
foch plugin enable dev.foch.eu4-dynamic-trade-blackhole --playset default

# Optional — switch between standard, gentle, assertive, observer, or sandbox:
uv run plugins/eu4-dynamic-trade-blackhole/tools/presets.py --playset default --preset standard
[/code]

[h3]Step 3 — Launch EU4 Through Foch[/h3]
Start the game through Foch so the dynamic trade runtime attaches cleanly:
[code]
foch plugin launch --playset default
[/code]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Compatibility, Safety & Honest Status FAQ[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Which EU4 version is supported?[/b]
Strictly pinned to [b]EU4 v1.37.5 (Steam, Windows x64)[/b]. At startup, the plugin verifies the exact SHA-256 fingerprint of your [code]eu4.exe[/code]. If Paradox pushes a new update or you run a different executable build, the plugin [b]fails closed (refuses to load and stays completely inert)[/b]—meaning it will [b]never crash your game or corrupt your save files[/b] on an unsupported patch.

[*][b]Is this Ironman or Achievement compatible?[/b]
[b]No.[/b] Because Dynamic Trade Blackhole runs as a native runtime plugin launched via [code]foch plugin launch[/code] and alters core economic gameplay, Ironman mode and Steam Achievements are unavailable while any native plugin is loaded.

[*][b]Does it work in Multiplayer?[/b]
[b]Yes, with matching setups.[/b] Every player in the multiplayer lobby must launch EU4 through Foch using the [b]exact same plugin version and preset configuration[/b] so all clients evaluate identical monthly trade route flips and treasury fee payouts.

[*][b]Where do I see my Transit Fees and Source Bounties in-game?[/b]
Monthly Transit Fees and Source Bounties are deposited directly into each eligible nation's treasury on the monthly economy tick and update your [b]top-bar ducat counter immediately[/b]. Because EU4's vanilla budget ledger UI has fixed line-item categories, these payouts do not appear as a separate row inside the Economy tab's monthly balance breakdown, though every payout is logged in full detail in the Foch event log ([code]foch plugin status --run-dir <dir>[/code]).

[*][b]What is the current testing and verification status?[/b]
We believe in 100% transparency with players:
[list]
[*][b]Live-Verified in 800-Day EU4 1.37.5 Soak Tests:[/b] Monthly economy hook stability, reversible route closures and reopenings (e.g., tax-developed Nippon sealing its outgoing leak at month 8; developed [code]Hangzhou -> Xi'an[/code] recovering from [code]-1.9%[/code] to [code]+24.1%[/code] net flow and reopening at month 22), and monthly treasury role-fee payouts (Malacca retaining [b]48.5[/b] vs. [b]34.9[/b] trade value and advancing a full treasury bracket over 26 months) are verified in live game sessions.
[*][b]In Progress Before v1.0 Release:[/b] The newest shared dataplane update (automatic runtime member-province discovery with [code]node_members.txt[/code] fallback), the 5-preset switcher, and the expanded [b]World Trade Hub Gazette[/b] (with 12-month moving-average scoring and structured receipts) have passed comprehensive unit tests and offline end-to-end validation ([code]foch test --no-run[/code]) and are currently undergoing final live in-game re-verification prior to tagging the v1.0 release.
[/list]
[/list]

